--- TEST: SYN-005
--- Area: Syntax
--- Priority: high
--- Name: .terminal !write works inside function bodies
--- Expect:
---   In 4.4 the directive compiled to nothing (the compiler had no
---   write branch for TerminalCommand), so terminal UIs rendered blank
---   frames. Written text has no trailing newline and must appear from
---   top level, from a function, and from a JIT-hot function (60 calls).

func draw() {
    .terminal !write "W";
}

i: i = 0;
while (i < 60) do
    draw();
    i = i + 1;
end

.terminal !write "|";
>! " [SYN-005-1] PASS — 61 writes executed, program reached the end";
